I don't believe it's possible without adding new metadata tables, and I don't believe that's a bad thing.  The last time new tables got added, it was a massive leap forward, probably the best thing that's ever happened to the CLR.  But that was 18 years ago, and as far as I'm aware there have been no IL or metadata changes since.  The .NET 2.0 CLR architecture is starting to show its age now, and we really need to be open to the idea of more additions.

